  "details": "I'm not sure if it was reduced to help serverside computation, but the ～10hz update rate of avatar parameters and ik and so on is egregious.  If it was changed just for quest, then change it back so pc can have high fidelity tracking and quest can have trimmed signal.\n\nThere should be a way to either have it drastically improve in unpopulated lobbies; or give an option to override it to a higher update rate.\n\nFor example: if i set mine to 60hz, i should be able to send and receive 60hz so long as others are also set to 60hz, anyone who has less should have the signal trimmed to their own maximum rate before it is sent out to them, and i'd only receive the highest they output.\n\nHave the default be highly variable, so it goes down to 10hz in 60+ instances, but goes up to 60hz in like 10 or less member instances; whilst having overrides as well if you want always low or always high update (auto,10,30,60hz).",
